      "message": "Sorry my mistake. `asyncWait.busyWait()` calls `Tick()` in a loop until the submit fence is passed and `MapAsync()` callback is called. It doesn\u0027t use `vkWaitForFence()`. So actually, it is worse than using it.\n\nFor this `DawnBuffer` use case, because the buffer is used for data transfer already, so I assume the `wgpu::Buffer` is not in CPU host stage. So `MapAsync()` must put a pipeline barrier to transfer it to CPU host stage[1]. so the following `Tick()` call has to submit the pending command buffer with barrier, right?\nIf a frame needs modify multiple `DawnBuffer`s, the cost should be bigger comparing to calling `MapAsync()`s in advance, so barriers can be submitted together instead of multiple `vkQueueSubmit()` calls. Assuming `vkQueueSubmit()` is expensive.\n\n[1] https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/vulkan/BufferVk.cpp;l\u003d315;drc\u003d1b9dea23074ba65c0f16113bb22848e2c579f193;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d1",
